  Public API from [38;5;153mcreatePreferences(backend)[39m:
  - [38;5;153mget(key)[39m — returns the stored value, or the declared default if absent, invalid, or unparseable. Throws on an
    unknown key (typo protection).
  - [38;5;153mset(key, value)[39m — validates against the schema, throws on unknown key or failed validation, otherwise persists
    immediately.
  - [38;5;153mreset(key)[39m / [38;5;153mreset()[39m — restore one key or all keys to defaults.
  - [38;5;153mall()[39m — a plain object of every key's effective value.

  [1mBackends.[0m A backend is any object with [38;5;153mgetItem(key)[39m / [38;5;153msetItem(key, value)[39m / [38;5;153mremoveItem(key)[39m. [38;5;153mlocalStorageBackend()[39m
  returns [38;5;153mwindow.localStorage[39m after a probe write (a [38;5;153mtry/catch[39m round-trip on a throwaway key, which is the only reliable
  way to detect Safari private mode and disabled storage); if the probe fails it returns [38;5;153mmemoryBackend()[39m instead, so
  the app runs with prefs that simply don't survive the session rather than crashing.

  [1mPersistence format.[0m One [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m key, [38;5;153m"preferences"[39m, holding a JSON object of the known keys only. Unknown keys
  found in stored JSON are ignored on read and dropped on the next write.

  [1mModule export.[0m [38;5;153mpreferences.js[39m ends with a dual export — [38;5;153mif (typeof module !== "undefined" && module.exports) { [39m
  [38;5;153mmodule.exports = {...} } else { window.Preferences = {...} }[39m — so the same file is a plain script in the browser and a
  [38;5;153mrequire[39m-able CommonJS module under [38;5;153mnode:test[39m, with no build step and no [38;5;153m"type": "module"[39m change that would break
  [38;5;153msrc/[39m.

  [1mThe password is never a schema key.[0m There is no code path that can persist it, and a test asserts the serialized blob
  never contains a [38;5;153mpassword[39m field.

